From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: single 2D ASTC textures leave out their top mip levels (EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D), off by default

What: the TrimmedLevels path (host mip 0 = guest mip N), so far used only by the opt-in array rule
EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB, now also takes single 2D ASTC textures. A texture with one layer, one
sample, depth 1 and at least 2 levels, that the older rules left whole, loses its top level, then
the next, while its largest kept side is over DIM texels and its kept levels, as RGBA8, are over
MIB, up to N levels; at least one level is always kept, and a texture with only one level is never
trimmed (that protects most UI and text). TranscodeAstcToBcn works on the trimmed shape: decode
image, encode and copies use the host size, AssembleInto(info, skip, ...) (the decoder already
supports a skip). A trimmed image skips the EDEN_UP_ASTC_BATCH_MIB batching (planned on the
guest's levels). Each image keeps its own saved bytes (Image::trim_2d_held, vk_texture_cache.h) on
a "held" total, handed over on a move and taken off once when the image goes; unbacked images
count 0.

Switches (read once): EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D=<N> (unset or 0 off; 1 at most one top level; 9 no level
limit, as upstream); EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D_DIM (texels, unset 1024); EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D_MIB (MiB,
unset 8); EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D_CHECK=1 (count only, trim nothing).
Log (Render_Vulkan): at first use "EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D=N: single 2D ASTC over D texels and M MiB
decoded lose up to N top levels[ (check: counted only)]"; every 10 s while on "EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D
10s: mode apply|check, images N, host saved X MiB, held H MiB (peak P), decode image saved Z MiB,
largest side S". Judge by held and peak (what exists now), not by images or host saved (the same
textures are made again and again).

Store stamp: the four names are in TranslationSwitches (vk_pipeline_prep.cpp); unset they do not
enter the stamp, set they give each arm its own kept-shader store (first run of an arm is cold).

Cost when off: one test of a static in TrimmedHostInfo, the image constructor and TickFrame; each
image is 8 bytes larger and its move or destroy does one "is it 0" test. No line, nothing
allocated, nothing trimmed; skip is 0 in TranscodeAstcToBcn, so that path is as before.

Risks: blurrier large textures up close (the trade); a shader asking for a level by number or for
the texture's size gets the smaller copy (look for shifted, half-size or wrongly tiled textures in
clips); minimap or HUD textures over 1024 with mips could change what STEER and the video checks
see (one STEER route in the apply arm first). With EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LAYERS=1 the apply-mode
counter also credits single-layer trims the NX2 rule made. held can run a few frames ahead of the
census at area changes (images waiting to be freed).

Origin and credit: idea and thresholds (1024 texels / 8 MiB decoded, top mip levels left out of
large single ASTC textures) from pablotz, NotRexed/Hookshot e460da1dd5 "perf(vk): reduce ASTC
memory pressure on small VRAM budgets" (#1009), GPL-3.0. Adapted to Eden's TrimmedLevels path and
the GPU BC transcode; upstream acts only on its lowest preset with a small driver budget, ours is
the switch alone; the check mode and the held counter are ours. Draft
drafts-2026-11-11/ports-7/astc-small-vram/draft.v2.diff, placed unchanged (review fix: the counter
shows what is held, not a total of what was made).
